{% comment %}
  One review card. Extracted so the reviews section can render metaobjects and editor
  blocks through the same markup — otherwise the two paths drift apart the first time
  someone edits one of them.

  The star row is decorative; the rating is also exposed as text so a screen reader
  announces "Rated 5 out of 5" instead of five identical glyphs.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign stars = rating | default: 5 | round
-%}

<div class="st" aria-hidden="true">
  {%- for i in (1..stars) -%}★{%- endfor -%}
</div>
<span class="visually-hidden">Rated {{ stars }} out of 5</span>

{%- if title != blank -%}
  <h3 class="rcard__title">{{ title }}</h3>
{%- endif -%}

{%- if body != blank -%}
  <p>{{ body }}</p>
{%- endif -%}

<div class="who">
  {%- comment -%}
    The prototype drew an avatar as inline SVG per card. A single initial in a circle is
    the same visual weight, costs no extra markup per card, and avoids repeating a large
    SVG five times.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <span class="who__avatar" aria-hidden="true">{{ author | slice: 0 | upcase }}</span>
  <b>{{ author }}</b>
  {%- if context != blank -%}
    <span>· {{ context }}</span>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
